  "seen while reading (beside the registered reading)": "Practice with the cap at 8 and 12 taught the stack to recall one binding 150 to 200 bytes back (0.920 to 0.980), though it moved its age offsets by no more than 0.05 (diagnostic_age_offsets of practice_cap_raised.json): what changed lies in the tags and probes. So the errors of those runs' 20-hop chains at that distance (16.1% of the steps with the cap at 8) are not the distance alone; the chain that the model has written in between takes part. The runs with the cap at 16, whose rewards went more often to attempts without the right chain, recall less far (0.600 to 0.675).",
  "what follows": "As registered: recall falls with distance for chain-stack and four-stack and not for chain-tf and four-tf-chain, and the longer line does not explain it, so the next registration gives the stack's reads a measure of time in lines. The read's beats are not wired to streams (_StateRead._address: \"the clocks and pacemakers of a read are not wired to a stream yet\"), and every spiking run is trained and scored as a stream, so the clock takes the form of word heads that count lines (--read-word-unit line, commit 452f365): a line head reaches the present line alone, however long it is, and weighs its cells by their place in it, where a beat would have given a head an offset for the present line beside its offsets for age. This probe is one of its measures."
 }
